    │   exceptions instead of returning an rc code; amqtt is less actively maintained and has a different API surface (fork of hbmqtt) with its own 
    │   connect/publish coroutine signatures; connection error handling and reconnection semantics differ significantly across these libraries
    ├── Constraints: requires_connector
    └── paho-mqtt is used here as a synchronous, callback-based MQTT client to connect and publish JSON payloads to a broker. aiomqtt, gmqtt, and amqtt are all
        MQTT client libraries capable of the same connect/publish role, making them plausible substitutes for the underlying MQTT transport. The file's own 
        docstring explicitly calls out aiomqtt as a substitution target for paho-mqtt, confirming the intended equivalence.

